From: Guanyi Chen <felixlinker02@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] amdgpu: pin DMA-buf to VRAM instead of GTT

The upstream amdgpu driver pins DMA-buf exported buffers into GTT
(system memory), causing NVMe DMA addresses to point to CPU memory
instead of the GPU BAR. This defeats P2P DMA: data transits through
system memory rather than going directly between NVMe and GPU VRAM.

Pin to AMDGPU_GEM_DOMAIN_VRAM instead, and set
AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_CPU_ACCESS_REQUIRED to ensure the buffer lands in
visible VRAM (addressable via PCIe BAR).

After this patch, NVMe DMA addresses point to the GPU BAR
(e.g., 0x220xxxxxxxxx on MI210), enabling true PCIe P2P transfers.

Signed-off-by: Guanyi Chen <felixlinker02@gmail.com>
---
 amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_dma_buf.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_dma_buf.c b/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_dma_buf.c
index abcdef1..1234567 100644
--- a/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_dma_buf.c
+++ b/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_dma_buf.c
@@ -256,7 +256,9 @@
 	struct drm_gem_object *obj = attach->dmabuf->priv;
 	struct amdgpu_bo *bo = gem_to_amdgpu_bo(obj);
 
-	return amdgpu_bo_pin(bo, AMDGPU_GEM_DOMAIN_GTT);
+	/* pin into visible VRAM for P2P DMA via PCIe BAR */
+	bo->flags |= AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_CPU_ACCESS_REQUIRED;
+	return amdgpu_bo_pin(bo, AMDGPU_GEM_DOMAIN_VRAM);
 }
 
